const ARTICLES=[
['what','What Freemasonry Is','Foundations','Modern','official claim','Freemasonry is a lodge-based fraternal tradition that uses symbolic building language, moral allegory, fellowship and service.','Public explanations differ by jurisdiction, but regular Craft systems commonly organize members in local lodges under a Grand Lodge. The fraternity uses the language and tools of stonemasonry as moral symbols rather than as operative building credentials. UGLE describes Freemasonry as a social and charitable organization rooted in the traditions of medieval stonemasons.','ugle-what','lodge'],
['origins','Origins: Operative and Speculative Masonry','History','Medieval–1700s','scholarly','The exact origin of speculative Freemasonry is uncertain, but its language and imagery draw heavily on stonemason craft traditions.','Historians distinguish operative masonry, the actual building trade, from speculative Freemasonry, which uses building tools and lodge customs symbolically. Claims of uninterrupted institutional descent from antiquity should be treated as tradition unless supported by records.','ugle-history','hall'],
['ashmole','Elias Ashmole and 1646','History','1646','documented','Elias Ashmole recorded his initiation at Warrington in 1646, an important early record of an English speculative Mason.','UGLE cites Ashmole’s diary entry as the first recorded evidence of the initiation of an English speculative Mason, while also noting that others present must have been admitted earlier.','ugle-history','hall'],
['grandlodge1717','The Premier Grand Lodge, 1717','History','1717','documented','Four London lodges met on 24 June 1717 and formed what UGLE identifies as the world’s first Grand Lodge.','The meeting at the Goose and Gridiron Tavern elected Anthony Sayer as Grand Master. This institutional development is a major turning point in the history of organized modern Freemasonry.','ugle-history','hall'],
['constitutions','The 1723 Constitutions','History','1723','documented','The Constitutions of the Free-Masons provided rules, charges and a framework for the early Grand Lodge.','UGLE emphasizes the 1723 Constitutions for their role in shaping modern Freemasonry and for principles associated with the Enlightenment, including tolerance, civility, education and self-improvement.','ugle-1723','hall'],
['ireland-scotland','Ireland and Scotland Grand Lodges','History','1725–1736','documented','The Grand Lodge of Ireland was established in 1725 and the Grand Lodge of Scotland in 1736.','These institutions developed their own histories, practices and networks. Freemasonry has never been governed by one worldwide authority, which is why jurisdictional context matters throughout this app.','ugle-history','hall'],
['antients','Antients and Moderns','History','1751–1813','documented','A rival English Grand Lodge emerged in 1751 and called the original body the “Moderns,” while styling itself the “Antients.”','The two systems coexisted for decades and differed on aspects of practice. They united in 1813, creating the United Grand Lodge of England.','ugle-history','hall'],
['craft','Craft / Blue Lodge','Degrees','Modern','official claim','The foundational Craft degrees are Entered Apprentice, Fellowcraft and Master Mason.','These three degrees form the basic initiatory system in many Masonic jurisdictions. Appendant systems such as the Scottish Rite and York Rite build on the Master Mason degree but do not create a universal hierarchy in which a 32° or 33° Mason is “more of a Mason” than a Master Mason.','ugle-what','lodge'],
['officers','Common Lodge Officers','Lodge Life','Modern','official claim','Lodge officer structures vary, but many lodges include a Worshipful Master, Wardens, Deacons, Treasurer, Secretary and Tyler.','Titles, jewels and duties differ across jurisdictions. The Worshipful Master presides over the lodge; Wardens assist in governance; the Secretary and Treasurer manage records and finances; and the Tyler traditionally guards the outer door during tyled meetings.','ugle-what','lodge'],
['regalia','Regalia and Working Tools','Symbols','Modern','official claim','Aprons, collars, jewels, gavels, squares, levels and plumbs are among the most recognizable objects used in public Masonic imagery.','The meaning assigned to an object depends on ritual system and jurisdiction. Many items originated in the practical tools or clothing of operative stonemasons and were adapted into moral symbols.','ugle-what','lodge'],
['scottish','Scottish Rite Overview','Scottish Rite','1800s–present','official claim','The Scottish Rite confers additional degrees that expand on the first three Craft degrees.','In the Northern Masonic Jurisdiction, 29 degrees numbered 4° through 32° are arranged into four bodies: Lodge of Perfection, Council of Princes of Jerusalem, Chapter of Rose Croix and Consistory. The 33° is honorary and cannot be petitioned for.','sr-nmj','hall'],
['scottish1801','Charleston and the 1801 Supreme Council','Scottish Rite','1801','official claim','The Supreme Council of the Scottish Rite Southern Jurisdiction traces its establishment to Charleston, South Carolina, in 1801.','The Rite developed from earlier high-degree systems and later spread internationally. Northern and Southern Jurisdictions in the United States use related but not identical degree presentations and terminology.','sr-sj','hall'],
['york','York Rite Overview','York Rite','Modern','official claim','In the United States, the York Rite commonly includes Royal Arch Masonry, Cryptic Masonry and Masonic Knights Templar.','These bodies are organizationally distinct and requirements vary by jurisdiction. They should not be confused with the medieval Knights Templar as an uninterrupted historical institution.','ugle-what','lodge'],
['princehall','Prince Hall Freemasonry','Prince Hall','1775–present','documented','Prince Hall and fourteen other Black men were made Masons on 6 March 1775 in a military lodge attached to the 38th British Foot.','The Most Worshipful Prince Hall Grand Lodge of Massachusetts identifies this event as the beginning of Prince Hall Freemasonry in America. After the British military lodge departed, the group continued under limited permission and organized African Lodge.','princehall','prince'],
['africanlodge','African Lodge and the English Charter','Prince Hall','1776–1780s','documented','African Lodge developed under Prince Hall and later obtained an English charter.','The Prince Hall Grand Lodge’s public history explains that African Lodge was organized in 1776 and later petitioned the Grand Lodge of England for a warrant. This chartered tradition became foundational to Prince Hall Freemasonry.','african459','prince'],
['women','Women and Freemasonry','Women & Co-Masonry','1800s–present','official claim','Women’s Masonic and mixed-gender traditions exist, but recognition and eligibility rules differ sharply among Masonic systems.','The Order of Women Freemasons and Freemasonry for Women/HFAF are examples of women’s Masonic organizations in Britain. Co-Masonic systems admit multiple genders. Many mainstream male Grand Lodges do not recognize these bodies, so the app distinguishes membership practice from recognition.','owf','hall'],
['oes','Order of the Eastern Star','Affiliated Bodies','1800s–present','official claim','The Order of the Eastern Star is a Masonic-related fraternal organization rather than a Craft Grand Lodge.','Its official history credits Rob Morris with developing the system in the mid-19th century and describes the establishment of the General Grand Chapter in 1876. Eligibility and relationships to Masonry vary by jurisdiction.','oes','lodge'],
['shriners','Shriners International','Affiliated Bodies','1870–present','official claim','Shriners International is a fraternal organization historically associated with Master Masons and known publicly for philanthropy and Shriners Children’s.','The Shrine began in New York in 1870. Its fez and crescent-and-scimitar emblem are distinct from Craft Masonry’s square-and-compasses symbol.','shriner','hall'],
['youth','Masonic Youth Organizations','Affiliated Bodies','1900s–present','official claim','DeMolay International, Job’s Daughters International and the International Order of the Rainbow for Girls are youth organizations with Masonic relationships.','They are independent organizations with their own governance, eligibility rules and educational programs. Their connection to Masonry should not be treated as identical to Masonic lodge membership.','ugle-what','lodge'],
['recognition','Regularity and Recognition','Organization','Modern','official claim','Recognition is a relationship between sovereign Masonic jurisdictions, not a single worldwide certification issued by one central authority.','Grand Lodges decide which other Grand Lodges they recognize. Criteria can include territorial questions, belief requirements, membership rules and ritual landmarks. Recognition can change over time.','ugle-what','hall'],
['international','International Freemasonry','International','1700s–present','scholarly','Freemasonry spread worldwide and developed into multiple families of practice, including systems aligned with UGLE-style recognition and continental or liberal traditions.','Differences can concern belief requirements, discussion of politics or religion, membership eligibility and recognition. The app presents these distinctions descriptively rather than declaring one global standard.','ugle-history','hall'],
['religion','Religion and the Great Architect','Philosophy','Modern','official claim','Many Masonic systems use the expression “Great Architect of the Universe” as a non-sectarian title, but theological requirements vary.','Some Grand Lodges require belief in a Supreme Being; some continental or liberal Masonic bodies do not. Freemasonry is not itself one religion, and official bodies typically describe it as compatible with members retaining their own faiths.','ugle-what','lodge'],
['ethics','Moral Allegory and Self-Improvement','Philosophy','Modern','official claim','Masonic ceremonies use allegory, symbols and staged lessons to encourage reflection on character, duty, integrity and service.','The specific ritual wording is jurisdictional and much of it is reserved for members. This app limits ritual discussion to public descriptions and does not publish passwords, grips, signs or current private test material.','ugle-what','lodge'],
['charity','Charity and Public Service','Public Service','Modern','official claim','Charitable work is a major public-facing activity of many Masonic organizations.','Examples include local relief funds, scholarships, children’s health programs, dyslexia centers and community volunteering. Each charity should be evaluated through the organization that actually operates it rather than attributed generically to all Freemasonry.','sr-nmj','hall'],
['washington','George Washington and Freemasonry','People','1750s–1799','documented','George Washington’s Masonic membership is extensively documented by Masonic and archival institutions.','Washington’s association with Freemasonry became part of American civic imagery. When assessing specific ceremonial claims, the app links to the George Washington Masonic National Memorial and archival sources instead of relying on unsourced lists.','gwmem','washington'],
['franklin','Benjamin Franklin and Freemasonry','People','1700s','documented','Benjamin Franklin was active in colonial Freemasonry and published an American edition of Anderson’s Constitutions in Philadelphia in 1734.','Franklin is one of the best-documented early American Masons. Claims about any public figure are labeled confirmed, disputed or often claimed based on surviving evidence.','ugle-1723','franklin'],
['famous','How to Verify a “Famous Mason” Claim','Research','All eras','scholarly','Internet lists often repeat unverified claims about celebrities, politicians and historical figures.','A stronger method looks for lodge minutes, Grand Lodge records, membership certificates, correspondence, or responsible archival and scholarly sources. Absence of documentation does not prove non-membership, but rumor should never be promoted to fact.','loc','hall'],
['morgan','William Morgan Affair and Anti-Masonry','Controversies','1820s–1830s','documented','The disappearance of William Morgan after his threat to publish Masonic material triggered intense anti-Masonic activism in the United States.','The affair fueled a political movement, newspaper campaigns and the Anti-Masonic Party. Historical accounts should distinguish documented events from later conspiracy narratives.','loc','hall'],
['taxil','The Taxil Hoax','Controversies','1880s–1890s','documented','Léo Taxil promoted sensational anti-Masonic claims and later publicly admitted the deception.','The episode remains important because later conspiracy literature sometimes repeats elements detached from their hoax context. It is a useful case study in source criticism.','loc','hall'],
['illuminati','Freemasonry and the Illuminati','Myths vs Facts','1700s–present','scholarly','Freemasonry and the historical Bavarian Illuminati were different organizations, despite later conspiracy literature merging them.','Individuals and ideas sometimes moved through overlapping Enlightenment-era networks, but that does not establish a single continuous organization controlling modern Freemasonry. Claims of centralized world control require evidence beyond symbolic similarities.','ugle-history','hall'],
['dollar','Eye of Providence and the U.S. Dollar','Myths vs Facts','1780s–present','documented','The Eye of Providence is older than modern Freemasonry and is not proof that the U.S. Great Seal is a Masonic emblem.','Masons have used eye imagery, but symbols can have multiple historical traditions. A shared symbol does not by itself prove institutional authorship or control.','loc','hall'],
['dcstreets','Washington, D.C. Street-Plan Claims','Myths vs Facts','1790s–present','scholarly','Claims that Washington, D.C. streets were intentionally laid out as hidden Masonic symbols are popular online but require careful map and planning evidence.','The existence of diagonal avenues and geometric intersections does not by itself demonstrate a secret Masonic plan. Treat pattern-recognition claims cautiously and compare them with original planning documents.','loc','washington'],
['persecution','Freemasonry under the Nazi Regime','Persecution','1930s–1945','documented','The Nazi regime suppressed Masonic lodges, confiscated property and used anti-Masonic propaganda.','The United States Holocaust Memorial Museum documents the regime’s hostility toward Freemasonry and the seizure of lodge property and archives. This history is better documented than many exaggerated numerical claims circulated online.','ushmm','hall'],
['architecture','Masonic Architecture and Temples','Architecture','1700s–present','documented','Masonic halls range from modest local lodge buildings to monumental civic architecture.','Freemasons’ Hall in London and the George Washington Masonic National Memorial in Alexandria are major public examples. Buildings often use classical, Egyptian, Gothic or Art Deco vocabularies depending on period and place.','nps','memorial'],
['research','How This App Handles Evidence','Research','Current','scholarly','Every topic should be read with its evidence label, jurisdiction note and source list.','“Documented” means supported by records or strong historical evidence. “Official claim” means an organization’s own public description. “Scholarly” signals interpretation. “Legend” identifies traditional narratives, while “disputed” marks contested or unverified claims.','loc','hall']
].map(a=>({id:a[0],title:a[1],category:a[2],era:a[3],evidence:a[4],summary:a[5],body:a[6],source:a[7],photo:a[8],reviewed:'2026-10-09'}));
const DEGREE_NAMES=['Builder','Perfect Master','Master of the Brazen Serpent','Provost and Judge','Intendant of the Building','Master of the Temple','Master Elect','Sublime Master Elected','Master of Mercy','Master of the Ninth Arch','Grand Elect Mason','Knight of the East','Prince of Jerusalem','Knight of the East and West','Knight of the Rose Croix of H. R. D. M.','Brothers of the Trail','Master Ad Vitam','Patriarch Noachite','Prince of Libanus','Knight of Valor','Brother of Tolerance','Master of Achievement','Friend & Brother Eternal','Knight of Jerusalem','Knight of the Sun','Knight of Saint Andrew','Grand Inspector',"My Brother's Keeper",'Sublime Prince of the Royal Secret'];
const DEGREES=DEGREE_NAMES.map((name,i)=>{const n=i+4;let body=n<=14?'Lodge of Perfection':n<=16?'Council of Princes of Jerusalem':n<=18?'Chapter of Rose Croix':'Consistory';return {n,name,body,summary:'A public NMJ degree in the '+body+'. The Northern Masonic Jurisdiction describes its degrees as dramatic allegories that expand on the ethical and philosophical lessons of the first three Craft degrees.'}});
const SYMBOLS=[['Square & Compasses','A central emblem of Freemasonry combining two traditional working tools; interpretations vary by jurisdiction.'],['Letter G','Common in some U.S. emblems; often associated with God, Geometry, or both, but not universal.'],['Eye of Providence','A much older religious and artistic symbol also used in some Masonic contexts.'],['24-inch Gauge','A working tool commonly interpreted as a lesson in ordering or dividing time.'],['Common Gavel','A tool adapted into moral symbolism about shaping or removing roughness.'],['Plumb','Commonly used as a symbol of upright conduct.'],['Level','Often interpreted as equality or the level condition of humanity.'],['Square','Commonly associated with ethical “squareness” or right conduct.'],['Trowel','A building tool that in some systems symbolizes spreading unity or brotherly affection.'],['Rough Ashlar','Unfinished stone used as an image of a person before moral refinement.'],['Perfect Ashlar','Finished stone used as an image of disciplined improvement.'],['Two Pillars','Architectural and biblical imagery associated with the entrance to Solomon’s Temple.'],['Checkered Pavement','Black-and-white flooring used in some lodge rooms; interpretations differ.'],['Acacia','A plant symbol appearing in Masonic funerary and immortality-related imagery.'],['Beehive','An emblem associated in some traditions with industry and cooperation.'],['Anchor and Ark','Older emblematic imagery appearing in some Masonic symbol systems.'],['Hourglass','A traditional emblem of passing time and mortality.'],['Scythe','A traditional emblem of mortality and the passage of life.'],['Blazing Star','A star emblem with varying interpretations across rituals and jurisdictions.'],['Cable-tow','A cord used symbolically in Masonic ritual; this app does not publish private ritual instructions.'],['Apron','Derived from operative work clothing and transformed into one of Masonry’s best-known pieces of regalia.'],['Gloves','Used in some jurisdictions and ceremonies, with historical links to operative craft clothing.'],['Tracing Boards','Illustrated teaching boards used especially in British and related Masonic traditions.'],['Point Within a Circle','A geometric emblem with multiple Masonic interpretations.'],['Sun, Moon and Stars','Celestial imagery used in architecture, ritual art and lodge decoration.'],["Jacob's Ladder",'Biblical ladder imagery used in some Masonic symbolic systems.'],['Corn, Wine and Oil','Traditional symbols associated with dedication and abundance in some ceremonies.'],['Keystone','A Royal Arch-related architectural symbol and a practical arch element.'],['Triple Tau','A prominent emblem associated with Royal Arch Masonry.'],['Double-Headed Eagle','A widely recognized emblem of the Scottish Rite in several jurisdictions.']].map((s,i)=>({id:'s'+i,name:s[0],meaning:s[1]}));
const GLOSSARY=[['Brother','A common fraternal form of address among Masons.'],['Lodge','A local body of Freemasons; also the room or building context in ordinary speech.'],['Grand Lodge','A sovereign Masonic governing body within its jurisdiction.'],['Grand Master','The presiding officer of a Grand Lodge.'],['Worshipful Master','The presiding officer of a Craft lodge in many jurisdictions.'],['Senior Warden','A senior lodge officer, often next in line after the Master.'],['Junior Warden','A principal lodge officer with duties varying by jurisdiction.'],['Deacon','A lodge officer role used in many systems.'],['Steward','An officer role often connected with hospitality or assistance.'],['Tyler / Tiler','An officer traditionally stationed outside the lodge door during a tyled meeting.'],['Tyled','Closed to non-authorized attendees under the rules of that lodge or jurisdiction.'],['Stated Communication','A regularly scheduled lodge meeting in many U.S. jurisdictions.'],['Charter / Warrant','Authority under which a lodge is constituted.'],['Dispensation','Temporary or special authority granted by an appropriate Masonic authority.'],['Petition','A formal request for membership or another action.'],['Ballot','A formal lodge vote, often used for membership decisions.'],['Candidate','A person seeking or receiving a degree.'],['Degree','A structured stage of initiation or instruction.'],['Working','A jurisdiction’s ritual or procedural form.'],['Jurisdiction','The territorial or organizational authority of a Masonic governing body.'],['Regularity','A concept used by Masonic bodies to judge conformity with their principles or landmarks.'],['Recognition','A formal relationship by which Masonic jurisdictions acknowledge each other.'],['Visitation','Attendance at another lodge under applicable recognition and eligibility rules.'],['Appendant Body','An organization associated with Masonry that generally requires prior Masonic qualification.'],['Concordant Body','A related fraternal body; usage varies.'],['Symbolic Lodge','Another term for Craft or Blue Lodge in many contexts.'],['Blue Lodge','Common U.S. term for the lodge conferring the first three Craft degrees.'],['Entered Apprentice','The first Craft degree in many Masonic systems.'],['Fellowcraft','The second Craft degree in many Masonic systems.'],['Master Mason','The third Craft degree and foundational status for many appendant bodies.'],['Past Master','A Mason who has previously served as Worshipful Master of a lodge.'],['Grand Secretary','Senior administrative officer of a Grand Lodge.'],['Orient','A term used in some Masonic systems for a geographic or administrative territory.'],['Valley','A Scottish Rite NMJ local/regional organizational term.'],['Supreme Council','A governing body used in Scottish Rite organization.'],['Consistory','In NMJ, the body covering the 19° through 32°.'],['Rose Croix','A Scottish Rite body/degree family; organization differs by jurisdiction.'],['Royal Arch','A major branch of York Rite and other Masonic systems.'],['Cryptic Masonry','A York Rite branch commonly organized in Councils in the U.S.'],['Commandery','A U.S. York Rite body conferring Masonic Templar orders.'],['Prince Hall Freemasonry','Historically Black Masonic traditions tracing to Prince Hall and African Lodge.'],['Profane','Historical Masonic usage for someone outside the fraternity; modern tone varies.'],['Light','A traditional metaphor for knowledge, insight or instruction.'],['Landmark','A principle considered fundamental by a Masonic jurisdiction; lists differ.'],['Grand Orient','A form of Masonic governing body used especially in continental traditions.']].map(g=>({term:g[0],definition:g[1]}));
const TIMELINE=[['Medieval period','Operative stonemason guilds, lodges and building traditions provide important vocabulary and imagery later used by speculative Freemasonry.'],['1646','Elias Ashmole records his initiation at Warrington.'],['1717','Four London lodges form the Premier Grand Lodge and elect Anthony Sayer.'],['1723','The Constitutions of the Free-Masons are published.'],['1725','Grand Lodge of Ireland established.'],['1734','Benjamin Franklin publishes an American edition of Anderson’s Constitutions in Philadelphia.'],['1736','Grand Lodge of Scotland established.'],['1751','The rival “Antients” Grand Lodge is formed in London.'],['1775','Prince Hall and fourteen other Black men are made Masons in a military lodge in Boston Harbor.'],['1776','African Lodge is organized under Prince Hall.'],['1784','African Lodge receives an English charter.'],['1813','Antients and Moderns unite to form the United Grand Lodge of England.'],['1820s','William Morgan affair helps ignite a major anti-Masonic movement in the United States.'],['1828','The Anti-Masonic Party emerges in U.S. politics.'],['1870','The fraternity that became Shriners International begins in New York.'],['1876','General Grand Chapter era of the Order of the Eastern Star begins.'],['1908','The Order of Women Freemasons traces its independent English organization to this period.'],['1930s–1945','Nazi authorities suppress lodges and confiscate Masonic property and archives.'],['20th century','Prince Hall recognition relationships with historically white Grand Lodges change significantly across U.S. jurisdictions.'],['21st century','Many Masonic organizations expand public websites, museums, archives and digital education.'],['2023','UGLE marks the tercentenary of the 1723 Constitutions.'],['2026','Masonic Atlas first public build assembled as an independent educational reference.']].map((t,i)=>({id:i,date:t[0],text:t[1]}));
const PEOPLE=[['George Washington','Confirmed','1732–1799','washington','First U.S. president; Masonic membership is extensively documented.','gwmem'],['Benjamin Franklin','Confirmed','1706–1790','franklin','Printer, scientist, diplomat and active colonial Mason.','ugle-1723'],['Prince Hall','Confirmed','c.1735–1807','prince','Founder associated with the beginnings of Prince Hall Freemasonry in America.','princehall'],['Rudyard Kipling','Confirmed','1865–1936','kipling','Writer whose Masonic affiliations are well documented.','loc'],['Arthur Conan Doyle','Confirmed','1859–1930','doyle','Author of Sherlock Holmes; documented member of Phoenix Lodge No. 257.','loc'],['Giuseppe Garibaldi','Confirmed','1807–1882','garibaldi','Italian nationalist leader with significant Masonic roles.','loc'],['Simón Bolívar','Documented / jurisdictional','1783–1830','bolivar','Often identified in Latin American Masonic history; verify specific lodge details by jurisdiction.','loc'],['Buzz Aldrin','Confirmed','1930–','aldrin','Apollo 11 astronaut and Freemason; public Masonic organizations document his membership.','loc'],['Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart','Confirmed','1756–1791','hall','Composer initiated in Vienna and associated with Masonic musical culture.','loc'],['John Theophilus Desaguliers','Confirmed','1683–1744','hall','Scientist, clergyman and important early Grand Lodge figure.','ugle-history'],['James Anderson','Confirmed / institutional','c.1679–1739','hall','Compiler associated with the 1723 Constitutions.','ugle-1723'],['Anthony Sayer','Confirmed','c.1672–1742','hall','Elected first Grand Master of the Premier Grand Lodge in 1717.','ugle-history'],['Rob Morris','Confirmed','1818–1888','hall','Freemason closely associated with developing the Order of the Eastern Star system.','oes'],['Christopher Wren','Often claimed','1632–1723','hall','Frequently claimed in older Masonic literature; modern evidence is contested.','ugle-history'],['Joseph Haydn','Disputed / limited','1732–1809','hall','Was admitted to a Viennese lodge, but the extent of later participation is debated.','loc']].map((p,i)=>({id:'p'+i,name:p[0],status:p[1],life:p[2],photo:p[3],bio:p[4],source:p[5]}));
const QUIZ=[{q:'Which are the three foundational Craft degrees?',a:['Entered Apprentice, Fellowcraft, Master Mason','Builder, Rose Croix, Consistory','Royal Arch, Cryptic, Shrine'],c:0,e:'The first three degrees are Entered Apprentice, Fellowcraft and Master Mason.'},{q:'What happened in London in 1717 according to UGLE?',a:['The first Grand Lodge was formed','The Scottish Rite began','African Lodge was chartered'],c:0,e:'Four London lodges formed the Premier Grand Lodge on 24 June 1717.'},{q:'How many Scottish Rite NMJ degrees are numbered 4° through 32°?',a:['29','30','33'],c:0,e:'There are 29 additional degrees from 4° through 32°.'},{q:'Can a Mason petition for the NMJ 33°?',a:['No, it is honorary','Yes, after one year','Only through a Blue Lodge ballot'],c:0,e:'NMJ describes the 33° as an honorary degree awarded by Supreme Council.'},{q:'Who is central to the origin of Prince Hall Freemasonry?',a:['Prince Hall','Anthony Sayer','James Anderson'],c:0,e:'Prince Hall and fourteen other Black men were made Masons in 1775.'},{q:'Does one worldwide authority govern all Freemasonry?',a:['No','Yes, UGLE','Yes, the Scottish Rite'],c:0,e:'Grand Lodges and other Masonic systems are sovereign within their own jurisdictions.'},{q:'Is the Eye of Providence uniquely Masonic?',a:['No','Yes','Only in the United States'],c:0,e:'The symbol predates modern Freemasonry and appears in broader religious and artistic traditions.'},{q:'What is the app’s rule on private ritual material?',a:['Do not publish passwords, grips, signs or current private tests','Publish everything online','Only publish if anonymous'],c:0,e:'This app is a public-history reference, not an exposure of current private ritual.'}];
const state={view:'home',detail:null,query:'',category:'All',bookmarks:new Set(store.get('bookmarks',[])),theme:store.get('theme','dark'),font:store.get('font',1)};let installPrompt=null;
function src(id){return SOURCES.find(s=>s.id===id)||SOURCES[0]}function esc(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,m=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[m]))}function photoTag(id,alt){const p=photo(id);return '<img loading="lazy" src="'+p.url+'" alt="'+esc(alt||p.title)+'">'}function badgeEvidence(e){return '<span class="badge gold">'+esc(e)+'</span>'}
function setView(v){state.view=v;state.detail=null;state.query='';location.hash=v;render();window.scrollTo(0,0)}function toggleBookmark(id){state.bookmarks.has(id)?state.bookmarks.delete(id):state.bookmarks.add(id);store.set('bookmarks',[...state.bookmarks]);render()}function openArticle(id){state.detail=id;state.view='article';location.hash='article='+id;render();window.scrollTo(0,0)}
function topShell(content){const nav=[['home','Home'],['explore','Explore'],['degrees','Degrees'],['symbols','Symbols'],['people','People'],['gallery','Real Pictures'],['timeline','Timeline'],['glossary','Glossary'],['quiz','Quiz'],['sources','Sources'],['bookmarks','Bookmarks']];return '<div class="shell"><aside class="sidebar"><div class="brand"><img src="./icon.svg" alt=""><div><h1>Masonic Atlas</h1><small>Freemasonry Encyclopedia</small></div></div><nav class="nav">'+nav.map(n=>'<button data-view="'+n[0]+'" class="'+(state.view===n[0]?'active':'')+'">'+n[1]+'</button>').join('')+'</nav><div class="side-tools"><button class="tool-btn" id="themeBtn">'+(state.theme==='dark'?'Light':'Dark')+'</button><button class="tool-btn" id="fontBtn">Text +</button></div></aside><main class="main"><header class="topbar"><div class="search"><span>⌕</span><input id="globalSearch" placeholder="Search history, degrees, symbols, people…" value="'+esc(state.query)+'"></div><button class="install" id="installBtn">Install App</button></header><div class="content">'+content+'</div></main></div><nav class="bottom-nav">'+[['home','Home'],['explore','Explore'],['gallery','Photos'],['quiz','Quiz'],['bookmarks','Saved']].map(n=>'<button data-view="'+n[0]+'" class="'+(state.view===n[0]?'active':'')+'">'+n[1]+'</button>').join('')+'</nav>'}
function articleCard(a){const saved=state.bookmarks.has(a.id);return '<article class="card"><div class="card-img">'+photoTag(a.photo,a.title)+'</div><div class="card-body"><div class="meta"><span class="badge">'+esc(a.category)+'</span>'+badgeEvidence(a.evidence)+'</div><h4>'+esc(a.title)+'</h4><p>'+esc(a.summary)+'</p><div class="card-actions"><button class="small-btn" data-open="'+a.id+'">Read</button><button class="small-btn '+(saved?'saved':'')+'" data-save="'+a.id+'">'+(saved?'Saved':'Save')+'</button></div></div></article>'}
function home(){const featured=['what','grandlodge1717','princehall','scottish','persecution','architecture'].map(id=>ARTICLES.find(a=>a.id===id));return '<section class="hero">'+photoTag('lodge','Masonic lodge room')+'<div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public history • sourced • jurisdiction-aware</div><h2>Explore Freemasonry with evidence, context and real archival media.</h2><p>Masonic Atlas is an independent educational reference covering history, degrees, symbols, people, organizations, architecture, controversies and primary-source pathways. It does not claim affiliation with any Grand Lodge.</p><div class="hero-actions"><button class="primary" data-view="explore">Start Exploring</button><button class="secondary" data-view="gallery">View Real Pictures</button></div></div></section><div class="notice"><b>Evidence rule:</b> official organizational descriptions, documented history, scholarly interpretation, legend and disputed claims are labeled separately.</div><div class="section-head"><div><h3>Featured knowledge</h3><p>Core topics to start with.</p></div></div><div class="grid">'+featured.map(articleCard).join('')+'</div><div class="section-head"><div><h3>Quick routes</h3><p>Jump into the major reference collections.</p></div></div><div class="grid grid-4">'+[['Degrees','29 NMJ Scottish Rite degrees plus Craft overview','degrees'],['Symbols','30 public symbol explanations','symbols'],['People','Verified and qualified membership claims','people'],['Timeline','From operative roots to the present','timeline']].map(x=>'<button class="card card-body small-btn" data-view="'+x[2]+'"><h4>'+x[0]+'</h4><p>'+x[1]+'</p></button>').join('')+'</div>'}
function explore(){let cats=['All',...new Set(ARTICLES.map(a=>a.category))];let list=ARTICLES.filter(a=>(state.category==='All'||a.category===state.category)&&(!state.query||((a.title+' '+a.summary+' '+a.body+' '+a.category).toLowerCase().includes(state.query.toLowerCase()))));return '<h2 class="page-title">Encyclopedia</h2><p class="page-lead">Browse the first-release knowledge base. Every article shows an evidence classification, a last-reviewed date and a source pathway.</p><div class="filters"><select id="catFilter">'+cats.map(c=>'<option '+(state.category===c?'selected':'')+'>'+esc(c)+'</option>').join('')+'</select><span class="badge">'+list.length+' articles</span></div><div class="grid">'+list.map(articleCard).join('')+'</div>'}
function article(){const a=ARTICLES.find(x=>x.id===state.detail);if(!a)return explore();const s=src(a.source),p=photo(a.photo);return '<article class="article"><button class="secondary" data-view="explore">← Back to encyclopedia</button><div class="meta" style="margin-top:18px"><span class="badge">'+esc(a.category)+'</span><span class="badge">'+esc(a.era)+'</span>'+badgeEvidence(a.evidence)+'</div><h2 class="page-title">'+esc(a.title)+'</h2><p class="page-lead">'+esc(a.summary)+'</p><div class="article-hero">'+photoTag(a.photo,a.title)+'</div><div class="article-body"><p>'+esc(a.body)+'</p><h3>Jurisdiction note</h3><p>Freemasonry is organized through sovereign jurisdictions and related bodies. Terminology, recognition, ritual wording, membership rules and officer structures can differ. This article is a public overview, not a universal ritual rule.</p><h3>Private material policy</h3><p>Masonic Atlas does not publish current passwords, grips, signs, test questions or private ritual text. Historical exposures may be discussed as historical documents without reproducing current secret work.</p></div><div class="section-head"><div><h3>Sources & media credits</h3></div></div><div class="source-list"><div class="source-row"><strong>'+esc(s.org)+' — '+esc(s.name)+'</strong><span>'+esc(s.note)+'</span><br><a href="'+s.url+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source</a></div><div class="source-row"><strong>Image: '+esc(p.title)+'</strong><span>'+esc(p.credit)+' • '+esc(p.rights)+'</span><br><a href="'+p.source+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Image source / license</a></div></div><p class="page-lead">Last reviewed: '+a.reviewed+'</p></article>'}
function degrees(){return '<h2 class="page-title">Degrees</h2><p class="page-lead">The Craft degrees — Entered Apprentice, Fellowcraft and Master Mason — are foundational. The Scottish Rite NMJ publicly lists 29 additional degrees, 4°–32°, organized into four bodies. The 33° is honorary and cannot be petitioned for.</p><div class="notice"><b>NMJ organization:</b> Lodge of Perfection 4°–14° • Council of Princes of Jerusalem 15°–16° • Chapter of Rose Croix 17°–18° • Consistory 19°–32°.</div><div class="degree-grid">'+DEGREES.map(d=>'<div class="degree"><div class="num">'+d.n+'°</div><h4>'+esc(d.name)+'</h4><small>'+esc(d.body)+'</small><p>'+esc(d.summary)+'</p></div>').join('')+'</div><div class="section-head"><div><h3>Primary degree source</h3></div></div><div class="source-row"><strong>Scottish Rite, Northern Masonic Jurisdiction</strong><span>Current public NMJ degree list and explanations.</span><br><a href="https://scottishritenmj.org/degrees" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open official source</a></div>'}
function symbols(){return '<h2 class="page-title">Symbols Encyclopedia</h2><p class="page-lead">Symbols rarely have only one fixed meaning across every jurisdiction. These entries give public, high-level interpretations and flag common overclaims.</p><div class="symbol-grid">'+SYMBOLS.map(s=>'<div class="symbol"><h4>'+esc(s.name)+'</h4><p>'+esc(s.meaning)+'</p></div>').join('')+'</div>'}
function people(){return '<h2 class="page-title">People</h2><p class="page-lead">Profiles are labeled to separate confirmed membership from disputed, limited or often-repeated claims.</p><div class="people-grid">'+PEOPLE.map(p=>'<article class="card person">'+photoTag(p.photo,p.name)+'<div class="card-body"><span class="badge gold">'+esc(p.status)+'</span><h4>'+esc(p.name)+'</h4><small>'+esc(p.life)+'</small><p>'+esc(p.bio)+'</p><p><a href="'+src(p.source).url+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source pathway</a></p></div></article>').join('')+'</div>'}
function gallery(){return '<h2 class="page-title">Real Pictures & Archival Media</h2><p class="page-lead">No AI illustrations in this gallery. Every image points to its original archive or Commons file page so you can inspect creator and rights information.</p><div class="gallery">'+PHOTOS.map(p=>'<figure class="photo"><button class="small-btn" style="padding:0;border:0" data-photo="'+p.id+'">'+photoTag(p.id,p.title)+'</button><figcaption><b>'+esc(p.title)+'</b><br>'+esc(p.credit)+'<br>'+esc(p.rights)+'</figcaption></figure>').join('')+'</div>'}
function timeline(){return '<h2 class="page-title">Timeline</h2><p class="page-lead">A high-level chronology. Dates tied to organizational self-history are linked back to the source center.</p><div class="timeline">'+TIMELINE.map(t=>'<div class="timeline-item"><span class="badge gold">'+esc(t.date)+'</span><p>'+esc(t.text)+'</p></div>').join('')+'</div>'}
function glossary(){return '<h2 class="page-title">Glossary</h2><p class="page-lead">Common public Masonic terms. Usage can vary by jurisdiction.</p><div class="glossary">'+GLOSSARY.map(g=>'<div class="term"><b>'+esc(g.term)+'</b><div>'+esc(g.definition)+'</div></div>').join('')+'</div>'}
function quiz(){return '<h2 class="page-title">Learn / Quiz</h2><p class="page-lead">Tap an answer to see the explanation immediately.</p><div class="quiz">'+QUIZ.map((q,i)=>'<div class="question"><b>'+(i+1)+'. '+esc(q.q)+'</b><div class="answers">'+q.a.map((a,j)=>'<button class="answer" data-q="'+i+'" data-a="'+j+'">'+esc(a)+'</button>').join('')+'</div><div id="ex'+i+'" class="explain hidden"></div></div>').join('')+'</div>'}
function sources(){return '<h2 class="page-title">Source Center</h2><p class="page-lead">The app prioritizes official organizations for their own rules and self-descriptions, archives for primary material, and museum/scholarly sources for independent historical context.</p><div class="source-list">'+SOURCES.map(s=>'<div class="source-row"><span class="badge">'+esc(s.type)+'</span><strong>'+esc(s.org)+' — '+esc(s.name)+'</strong><span>'+esc(s.note)+'</span><br><a href="'+s.url+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source</a></div>').join('')+'</div><div class="section-head"><div><h3>Media credits</h3></div></div><div class="source-list">'+PHOTOS.map(p=>'<div class="source-row"><strong>'+esc(p.title)+'</strong><span>'+esc(p.credit)+' • '+esc(p.rights)+'</span><br><a href="'+p.source+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open image source</a></div>').join('')+'</div>'}
function bookmarks(){const list=ARTICLES.filter(a=>state.bookmarks.has(a.id));return '<h2 class="page-title">Bookmarks</h2><p class="page-lead">Saved on this device.</p>'+(list.length?'<div class="grid">'+list.map(articleCard).join('')+'</div>':'<div class="empty">No saved articles yet.</div>')}
function searchResults(){const q=state.query.trim().toLowerCase();if(!q)return home();const arts=ARTICLES.filter(a=>(a.title+' '+a.summary+' '+a.body+' '+a.category).toLowerCase().includes(q));const syms=SYMBOLS.filter(s=>(s.name+' '+s.meaning).toLowerCase().includes(q));const terms=GLOSSARY.filter(g=>(g.term+' '+g.definition).toLowerCase().includes(q));const peeps=PEOPLE.filter(p=>(p.name+' '+p.bio+' '+p.status).toLowerCase().includes(q));return '<h2 class="page-title">Search</h2><p class="page-lead">Results for “'+esc(state.query)+'”</p><div class="grid">'+arts.map(articleCard).join('')+'</div>'+(syms.length?'<div class="section-head"><h3>Symbols</h3></div><div class="symbol-grid">'+syms.map(s=>'<div class="symbol"><h4>'+esc(s.name)+'</h4><p>'+esc(s.meaning)+'</p></div>').join('')+'</div>':'')+(peeps.length?'<div class="section-head"><h3>People</h3></div><div class="glossary">'+peeps.map(p=>'<div class="term"><b>'+esc(p.name)+'</b><div>'+esc(p.bio)+'</div></div>').join('')+'</div>':'')+(terms.length?'<div class="section-head"><h3>Glossary</h3></div><div class="glossary">'+terms.map(g=>'<div class="term"><b>'+esc(g.term)+'</b><div>'+esc(g.definition)+'</div></div>').join('')+'</div>':'')+(!arts.length&&!syms.length&&!peeps.length&&!terms.length?'<div class="empty">No matches found.</div>':'')}
function render(){document.body.classList.toggle('light',state.theme==='light');document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--font-scale',state.font);let body=state.query&&state.view!=='article'?searchResults():state.view==='home'?home():state.view==='explore'?explore():state.view==='article'?article():state.view==='degrees'?degrees():state.view==='symbols'?symbols():state.view==='people'?people():state.view==='gallery'?gallery():state.view==='timeline'?timeline():state.view==='glossary'?glossary():state.view==='quiz'?quiz():state.view==='sources'?sources():bookmarks();app.innerHTML=topShell(body);bind()}
function bind(){document.querySelectorAll('[data-view]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>setView(b.dataset.view));document.querySelectorAll('[data-open]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>openArticle(b.dataset.open));document.querySelectorAll('[data-save]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>toggleBookmark(b.dataset.save));const s=$('#globalSearch');if(s)s.oninput=e=>{state.query=e.target.value;setTimeout(render,80)};const f=$('#catFilter');if(f)f.onchange=e=>{state.category=e.target.value;render()};const t=$('#themeBtn');if(t)t.onclick=()=>{state.theme=state.theme==='dark'?'light':'dark';store.set('theme',state.theme);render()};const ft=$('#fontBtn');if(ft)ft.onclick=()=>{state.font=state.font>=1.2?.9:Math.round((state.font+.1)*10)/10;store.set('font',state.font);render()};const ins=$('#installBtn');if(ins)ins.onclick=()=>{if(installPrompt){installPrompt.prompt();installPrompt.userChoice.finally(()=>installPrompt=null)}else alert('Use your browser menu and choose “Install app” or “Add to Home screen”.')};document.querySelectorAll('[data-photo]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>openPhoto(b.dataset.photo));document.querySelectorAll('[data-q]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>answer(Number(b.dataset.q),Number(b.dataset.a),b))}
function answer(qi,ai,btn){const q=QUIZ[qi],box=document.getElementById('ex'+qi);btn.parentElement.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((b,i)=>{b.disabled=true;if(i===q.c)b.classList.add('correct')});if(ai!==q.c)btn.classList.add('wrong');box.textContent=q.e;box.classList.remove('hidden')}
function openPhoto(id){const p=photo(id),lb=$('#lightbox');lb.innerHTML='<button class="lightbox-close" aria-label="Close">×</button><div class="lightbox-inner"><img src="'+p.url+'" alt="'+esc(p.title)+'"><div class="caption"><b>'+esc(p.title)+'</b><br>'+esc(p.credit)+' • '+esc(p.rights)+'<br><a href="'+p.source+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open original source / license</a></div></div>';lb.classList.remove('hidden');lb.querySelector('.lightbox-close').onclick=()=>lb.classList.add('hidden');lb.onclick=e=>{if(e.target===lb)lb.classList.add('hidden')}}
window.addEventListener('beforeinstallprompt',e=>{e.preventDefault();installPrompt=e});window.addEventListener('hashchange',()=>{const h=location.hash.slice(1);if(h.startsWith('article=')){state.view='article';state.detail=h.split('=')[1]}else if(h)state.view=h;render()});if('serviceWorker'in navigator)window.addEventListener('load',()=>navigator.serviceWorker.register('./sw.js'));const initial=location.hash.slice(1);if(initial.startsWith('article=')){state.view='article';state.detail=initial.split('=')[1]}else if(initial)state.view=initial;render();